.Z files are compressed using the compress utility.  You need to use
uncompress (which is the same program as compress) to use these files.
I got my version from gatekeeper.dec.com (I think).  The file was
compress-4.0-tar.  Of course, you would need tar to use that. 

If you ever need to find where anything is, telnet to
quiche.cs.mcgill.ca and login as archie.  Then, use prog <filename> to
get a list of ftp sites where you can find that file.

Hope this helps.  Good luck!
